- op: create  # dc1a
  at: '2026-04-08T22:41:25Z'  # dc1a
  by: agent  # dc1a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dc1a
  clock: 1  # dc1a
  nonce: dc1a  # dc1a
  data:  # dc1a
    kind: work_item  # dc1a
    title: "Tracker .ops YAML serializer corrupts long string scalars via nonce injection"  # dc1a
    status: todo_hard  # dc1a
    priority: 2  # dc1a
    parent:  # dc1a
    tags:  # dc1a
    - developer_experience  # dc1a
    before: []  # dc1a
    duplicate_of: []  # dc1a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # dc1a
    pr_ref:  # dc1a
    description: "**Symptom:** Updating any tracker item with a description (or other long string field) whose YAML-serialized representation exceeds ruamel.yaml's width threshold (4096) causes the per-line nonce comment to be embedded INSIDE the string value on read-back. The corrupted text appears as '  # <nonce>' literally inside the scalar. Observed 2026-04-08 on INV-gajap during a path correction that bumped the description from 3947 to ~4106 YAML bytes.\n\n**Root cause** (verified 2026-04-08 by reading store.py at HEAD):\n1. `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/store.py:289` sets `ry.width = 4096` on the ruamel.yaml dumper. This is intended to 'prevent line wrapping' but in fact only sets the SOFT line-length threshold for folded scalars; long double-quoted scalars containing strings whose YAML representation exceeds 4096 bytes get folded across multiple physical lines (newline + leading whitespace, which YAML reads back as a single space).\n2. `store.py:298-303` then post-processes the dumped YAML by appending '  # <nonce>' to EVERY non-empty physical line, INCLUDING physical lines that are continuations of a multi-line scalar.\n3. When CSafeLoader parses the file back at `store.py:316-333`, the appended comment is INSIDE the double-quoted string (since YAML treats '#' as literal inside quoted scalars), so the value comes back containing literal '  # <nonce>' text where the wrap point landed.\n\n**Reproduction:** create or update any item with a description whose UTF-8 byte length plus YAML overhead exceeds 4096 bytes. The bug fires deterministically. INV-gajap's first update attempt (4091 bytes + ~14 bytes YAML prefix) triggered '  # f084'; the second attempt (restructured paragraph) triggered '  # 418f' at the new wrap point.\n\n**Why it's structural and not cosmetic:**\n- Silently corrupts the in-memory state on every read after the affected op is recorded.\n- Fires on any future content addition to large items (the bf4oxh91w investigation items in particular average 3000-5000 bytes — they are one path-correction away from this bug).\n- The UI/JSON output shows the corrupted text, so consumers (humans and agents) act on bad data.\n- The corruption is invisible until you diff against intended text — agents will not notice they corrupted their own writes.\n\n**Proposed fixes** (in order of preference):\n\n1. **Skip continuation lines in the post-processor.** Track YAML scalar context while iterating `raw_yaml.split('\\n')` at store.py:296: any line whose first non-whitespace character continues a previously-opened double-quoted scalar must NOT receive the nonce comment append. Since the YAML serializer's output is structured, this is a parser-lite over the dumped text. ruamel guarantees indentation, so a continuation line is identifiable by its leading-whitespace + non-key prefix.\n\n2. **Force literal block scalars for description and other long fields.** Configure a ruamel.yaml representer that emits long strings as '|' (literal block) scalars, where each physical line becomes part of the scalar by indentation. The post-processor's line-by-line nonce append would then be visibly inside the scalar (preserving the bug) UNLESS the post-processor is also fixed — so this alone is not a fix, only a fix-enabler.\n\n3. **Raise width.** Setting `ry.width = 1_000_000` would suppress folding for any realistic description. Cheapest immediate mitigation. Risk: someone sometime will write a description over 1 million bytes (unlikely for descriptions, possible for fields containing pasted logs).\n\n4. **Combine 1 and 3:** raise width AND fix the post-processor. Belt and braces.\n\n**Tests to add:**\n- Round-trip test: create an item with a description of 5000 bytes containing multi-byte UTF-8 (em-dashes, arrows, ≈, →), verify show output matches input byte-for-byte.\n- Round-trip test: same for fields.<key> values of 5000 bytes.\n- Round-trip test: very long single-line descriptions (no embedded \\n) of 10000 bytes.\n- Regression test: literal '  # abcd' patterns in user input survive round-trip without being mistaken  # dc1a
      for a nonce on the next read.\n\n**Workaround until fixed:** keep description strings under ~4080 UTF-8 bytes (subtract YAML overhead from the 4096 ruamel width). Detail beyond that should go in discussion entries, which are stored as separate scalars and avoid the fold.\n\n**Discovered while:** updating INV-gajap (per-entry training-data cohort metadata) to correct stale 'on_transcript_change.py' file paths to '.agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py'. The fields.root_cause update (a short field) landed cleanly; the description update (long field) corrupted twice in different positions, both times at the ruamel fold boundary."  # dc1a
    fields: {}  # dc1a
